PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Core facts agreed by all: fish has Lyz:Halo-eGFP (neutrophils) + mpeg1:SNAP-DsRed (macrophages); supplied ligand is chloroalkane-Cy5 analog that covalently labels only HaloTag, adding ~630 nm-excitable fluorophore exclusively to neutrophils. Thus neutrophils carry both eGFP (488 nm) and Cy5 (630 nm); macrophages carry only DsRed (559 nm). 

Key split: (a) "first signals" = biological recruitment order after tailfin injury → neutrophils arrive first, so only 630 nm + 488 nm (D, supported by 1,8); (b) all three fluorophores present at imaging time → G (majority: 2,3,4,5,6,7,10,12,14,15); (c) "first" = recommended imaging sequence (longest λ first) → only 630 nm (A, 9,11). 

Unresolved: whether 559 nm signal could appear "early" via bleed-through or minor Cy5 shoulder after injury-induced pH shift. No data on time-resolved imaging or labeling efficiency. Will track which interpretation of "first" gains support in later rounds.}

